<!-- &#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472; SECTION 3 &#183; THE HONEST TRADE-OFF &#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472; -->
<section>
  <div class="vy-wrap-narrow">
    <span class="vy-eyebrow">The Honest Trade-Off</span>
    <h2>Minoxidil Isn't Wrong. It's Just Incomplete.</h2>
    <p>Minoxidil has decades of research behind it and it grows hair for a lot of men. That is not in dispute, and any page that tells you otherwise is selling you something. What it does not do is touch DHT. It widens blood vessels and keeps follicles in their growth phase longer, which is a real benefit, while the hormone shrinking those follicles carries on untouched.</p>
    <div class="vy-tradeoff-quotebox">So the question was never minoxidil or nothing. It's <em>"am I doing anything at all about the DHT underneath?"</em></div>
    <p>There is a second catch, and it is the practical one. Minoxidil is a topical you apply every day and never stop. Let it slide for a few months and the hair it was holding on to tends to go with it. A routine you abandon does less for your hair than a milder one you keep up. That is the whole case for a daily saw palmetto capsule: a real if more modest effect on DHT, no prescription, no known systemic side effects reported, and nothing to work into your scalp before bed.</p>

    <div class="vy-tri-grid">
      <div class="vy-tri-card">
        <h3><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 2l2.4 5.2 5.6.6-4.2 3.8 1.2 5.6L10 14.4l-5 2.8 1.2-5.6L2 7.8l5.6-.6L10 2z" fill="#125657"></path></svg>Direct regrowth</h3>
        <p>Minoxidil has the deepest clinical record for visible regrowth at the follicle. If that is your single criterion and a daily topical suits your routine, that route exists.</p>
        <span class="vy-who">Advantage: Minoxidil</span>
      </div>
      <div class="vy-tri-card">
        <h3><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M10 1.8c2.6 2 5.4 2.8 7.2 3 0 6.4-2.4 11-7.2 13.4C5.2 15.8 2.8 11.2 2.8 4.8c1.8-.2 4.6-1 7.2-3z" fill="#125657"></path><path d="M7 10l2.2 2.2L13.4 8" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>The DHT side</h3>
        <p>Minoxidil leaves DHT alone by design. Saw palmetto is what men add when they want the hormonal half of the picture covered too, without a prescription pad.</p>
        <span class="vy-who">Advantage: Saw Palmetto</span>
      </div>
