<!-- &#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472; SECTION 5 &#183; FAQ &#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472;&#9472; -->
<section class="vy-alt">
  <div class="vy-wrap">
    <div class="vy-section-head">
      <span class="vy-eyebrow">Straight Answers</span>
      <h2>Questions Men Ask Before Adding It</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="vy-faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Does saw palmetto do the same job as minoxidil?<span class="vy-chev"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M6 1v10M1 6h10" stroke="#125657" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="vy-faq-a"><b>No, and that is rather the point.</b> Minoxidil works at the follicle, widening blood vessels and holding hair in its growth phase longer. It has no known effect on DHT. Saw palmetto works on the hormonal side instead, more gently than a prescription DHT blocker, but on the actual driver. They answer two different questions, which is why plenty of men run both. Finasteride shows stronger DHT suppression in clinical research; saw palmetto's effect is real but more modest, with no prescription and no known systemic side effects reported of the kind associated with prescription DHT blockers.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I keep using minoxidil with this?<span class="vy-chev"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M6 1v10M1 6h10" stroke="#125657" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="vy-faq-a"><b>Yes, and that is the most common way men use it.</b> The two mechanisms do not overlap: minoxidil handles blood flow and the growth phase at the scalp, a DHT blocker handles the hormonal side. Nothing about the capsule asks you to give up your topical. As with any change to a routine, check with your healthcare provider if you have questions.</div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How long before I see results?<span class="vy-chev"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none"><path d="M6 1v10M1 6h10" stroke="#125657" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="vy-faq-a">Hair cycles are slow, and anyone promising you a date is overselling. Among customers who report results, less shedding is usually noticed first, often inside the first month or two, with visible thickness taking 90 days or more. The same slow clock applies to minoxidil and to the prescription options. Give any DHT-supportive routine at least 3 months of daily consistency, and the 365-day guarantee covers you while you make up your mind.</div>
      </details>
